**Current Requirements:**
```
SYSTEM OVERVIEW
===============
The system is a Role-based Access Control (RBAC) environment supporting multiple users, role hierarchies, temporary role delegation, revocation, and concurrent request processing. The system enforces authorization correctness, maintains delegation and permission consistency, and ensures safety and liveness under concurrency. Users have clearance levels (High, Medium, Low), and objects have classification levels (High, Medium, Low). Requests are classified by the highest classification level of affected objects and must comply with user clearance. Higher-clearance users can approve or reject lower-clearance user requests. Delegation and revocation of roles are governed by clearance and administrative rules. The system includes an Emergency Module to manage exceptional scenarios, which alters standard behaviors under specific triggers and constraints. Emergency mode is abstracted as a fixed duration but may terminate early if both administrators who activated it jointly deactivate it. The system must eventually return to Normal mode after Emergency mode.

EXISTING-SYSTEM ASSUMPTIONS AND CONSTRAINTS
============================================
- The set of administrators can range from 0 to 4, depending on scenario. Administrator uniqueness is based on set semantics; duplicate entries are not possible.
- Emergency mode can only be triggered from Normal mode and requires exactly two distinct administrators, acting jointly (no more, no fewer). Set-based uniqueness ensures that duplicates are not possible.
- Emergency mode is time-bounded, abstracted as a fixed duration; it may terminate early if both participating administrators jointly deactivate Emergency. The system must eventually return to Normal mode after Emergency mode.
- FIFO ordering for request processing can be bypassed only during Emergency mode, and only for high-classification requests.
- Mutual exclusivity of roles is suspended for all users only during Emergency mode. During Emergency mode, it must be possible for any user to simultaneously hold any combination of roles, including roles that are mutually exclusive in Normal mode.
- Emergency privilege is granted only to the two administrators who triggered Emergency mode (emAdmins), only during Emergency mode, and is revoked immediately at the conclusion of Emergency mode.
- Roles delegated during Emergency mode must be revoked when Emergency mode ends; specifically, any delegation assigned during Emergency mode must end at the first Normal state after Emergency ends. Roles delegated prior to Emergency mode are not automatically revoked, but may still expire or be revoked by an administrator during Emergency mode.
- Only the administrators who participated in the Emergency trigger (the two emAdmins) are required to update their credentials after Emergency mode ends.

PROSPECTIVE FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS
====================================
R1: Emergency Trigger  
Exactly two distinct administrators, while the system is in Normal mode, are required to jointly trigger entry into Emergency mode. No more and no fewer than two administrators may jointly trigger Emergency mode. Only these two participating administrators (emAdmins) are considered for all subsequent emergency-related requirements. Set-based uniqueness ensures that duplicates are not possible.

R2: Emergency Mode Duration  
Emergency mode is active only for a limited (bounded) time, abstracted as a fixed duration; however, it may terminate early if both participating administrators (emAdmins) jointly deactivate Emergency. The system must eventually return to Normal mode after Emergency mode.

R3: Emergency Mode Behavior  
R3.1. During Emergency mode, request processing may bypass FIFO order to prioritize and process multiple high-classification requests simultaneously.  
R3.2. During Emergency mode, mutual exclusivity of roles is suspended for all users. It must be possible for any user to simultaneously hold any combination of roles, including roles that are mutually exclusive in Normal mode.  
R3.3. During Emergency mode, only the two administrators who participated in the Emergency trigger (emAdmins) temporarily hold emergency privileges, and EmergencyPrivilege is granted only to them for the duration of Emergency mode.

R4: Post-Emergency Restoration  
R4.1. After Emergency mode ends, emergency privileges must be revoked from the two administrators (emAdmins) who participated in the Emergency trigger.  
R4.2. After Emergency mode ends, any roles delegated during Emergency mode must be revoked; specifically, any delegation assigned during Emergency mode must end at the first Normal state after Emergency ends. Delegated roles from before Emergency mode remain subject to normal expiration or administrator revocation, including during Emergency mode.  
R4.3. After Emergency mode ends, only the two administrators who participated in the Emergency trigger are required to update their credentials.

R5: Delegation Clearance  
Users with higher clearance may temporarily delegate one or more of their assigned roles to a lower-clearance user, provided that the delegate meets the role’s minimum clearance requirement.
```

[LESSON]: Alloy set semantics guarantee uniqueness, so duplicate membership cannot occur in sets; requirements and assertions about "no duplicates" need not be modeled directly.

[EVENT]: Syntax error from using sum over a Boolean in Alloy: Boolean expressions cannot be summed; the correct approach is to reason about set cardinality or restructure the relation.

[EVENT]: Ambiguity in mutual exclusion during Emergency resolved: requirement strengthened to explicitly require that all combinations of mutually exclusive roles must be possible and observable for any user in Emergency mode.

**Current Alloy Model:**
// ===================== RBAC Emergency Model [Alloy 6, MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE ROLES TESTABLE] =====================
// Abstract, verifiable, formal requirements model (structure, behavior, constraints)

// ======= OPEN STATEMENTS =======
open util/ordering[ClearanceLevel] as ClearanceOrd
open util/ordering[State] as Time

// ======= ENUMS AND MODES =======
abstract sig ClearanceLevel {}
one sig High, Medium, Low extends ClearanceLevel {}

abstract sig ClassificationLevel {}
one sig C_High, C_Medium, C_Low extends ClassificationLevel {}

abstract sig SystemMode {}
one sig Normal, Emergency extends SystemMode {}

// ======= CORE ENTITIES =======
sig User {
    clearance: one ClearanceLevel
}

sig Administrator in User {}

sig Role {
    mutuallyExclusiveWith: set Role,
    minClearance: one ClearanceLevel
}

sig Object {
    classification: one ClassificationLevel
}

sig Request {
    requestedBy: one User,
    affects: some Object,
    classification: one ClassificationLevel
}

sig Delegation {
    delegator: one User,
    delegatee: one User,
    role: one Role,
    delegatedAt: one State,
    expiresAt: lone State // None if non-expiring
}

sig EmergencyPrivilege {
    admin: one Administrator,
    grantedAt: one State,
    revokedAt: lone State
}

// ======= SYSTEM STATE =======
sig State {
    mode: one SystemMode,
    emAdmins: set Administrator,               // The two who triggered Emergency (empty in Normal)
    requests: set Request,
    delegations: set Delegation,
    emPrivs: set EmergencyPrivilege,
    needsCredentialUpdate: set Administrator
}

// ======= ADMINISTRATOR CARDINALITY CONSTRAINT (SCENARIO SPECIFIC) =======
fact AdminCountRange {
    // System-wide, number of Administrators is 0..4 (per scenario requirement)
    #Administrator >= 0 and #Administrator <= 4
}

// ======= EXISTING SYSTEM FACTS =======

// Admins always have High clearance
fact AdminDefinition {
    all a: Administrator | a.clearance = High
}

// Emergency mode: only triggered from Normal with exactly two distinct admins
fact EmergencyTriggerStrict {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Emergency) =>
            (#s.emAdmins = 2 and prevModeIsNormal[s] and all a: s.emAdmins | a in Administrator)
        else
            no s.emAdmins
}

// EmergencyPrivilege: only emAdmins, only during Emergency, granted at s
fact EmergencyPrivilegeAssignment {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Emergency) =>
            (all ep: s.emPrivs | ep.admin in s.emAdmins and ep.grantedAt = s and no ep.revokedAt)
        else
            no s.emPrivs
}

// Mutual exclusion enforced except during Emergency
fact MutualExclusionEnforced {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Normal) =>
            all u: User |
                all r1, r2: Role |
                    r1 != r2 and
                    r1 in rolesHeld[u, s] and r2 in rolesHeld[u, s] =>
                        not (r1 in r2.mutuallyExclusiveWith)
    // During Emergency, all users may hold mutually exclusive roles (no restriction)
}

// Role holding function
fun rolesHeld[u: User, s: State]: set Role {
    { r: Role |
        some d: s.delegations |
            d.delegatee = u and
            d.role = r and
            d.delegatedAt in pastOrEqual[s] and
            (no d.expiresAt or lt[s, d.expiresAt])
    }
}

// ======= TEMPORAL HELPERS =======
fun pastOrEqual[s: State]: set State { { s2: State | lte[s2, s] } }
fun past[s: State]: set State { { s2: State | lt[s2, s] } }
fun future[s: State]: set State { { s2: State | gt[s2, s] } }

// Highest classification of a set of objects
fun highestClass[os: set Object]: one ClassificationLevel {
    (some o: os | o.classification = C_High) => C_High
    else (some o: os | o.classification = C_Medium) => C_Medium
    else C_Low
}

// Request classification reflects highest classification of affected objects
fact RequestClassification {
    all req: Request |
        req.classification = highestClass[req.affects]
}

// FIFO enforced except for C_High requests during Emergency
fact FIFOEnforcedExceptEmergency {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Normal) => FIFOProcessing[s]
}

// FIFOProcessing is left abstract here; implementation not required for verification
pred FIFOProcessing[s: State] { }

// Emergency mode must eventually return to Normal mode (liveness)
fact EmergencyLiveness {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Emergency) =>
            some s2: future[s] | s2.mode = Normal
}

// Delegations assigned during Emergency are revoked at the first post-Emergency Normal state
fact EmergencyDelegationRevocation {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Normal and prevModeIsEmergency[s]) =>
            all d: Time/prev[s].delegations |
                (d.delegatedAt.mode = Emergency) => (d.expiresAt = s)
}

// Delegations assigned before Emergency are NOT auto-revoked
fact PreEmergencyDelegationsRemain {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Normal and prevModeIsEmergency[s]) =>
            all d: Time/prev[s].delegations |
                (d.delegatedAt.mode = Normal) =>
                    (no d.expiresAt) or (d.expiresAt != s)
}

// Only emAdmins from previous Emergency must update credentials after Emergency ends
fact EmergencyCredentialUpdate {
    all s: State |
        ((s.mode = Normal and prevModeIsEmergency[s]) =>
            (Time/prev[s].emAdmins in s.needsCredentialUpdate and
             all a: s.needsCredentialUpdate | a in Time/prev[s].emAdmins)
        )
}

// EmergencyPrivilege is revoked immediately after Emergency ends
fact EmergencyPrivilegeRevocation {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Normal and prevModeIsEmergency[s]) =>
            no s.emPrivs
}

// ======= DELEGATION CLEARANCE WITH TOTAL ORDERING =======
// Only higher-clearance users may delegate to lower-clearance users, and delegatee must meet role minClearance
fact DelegationClearance {
    all s: State, d: s.delegations |
        not ClearanceOrd/lt[d.delegator.clearance, d.delegatee.clearance]
        and ClearanceOrd/lte[d.delegatee.clearance, d.role.minClearance]
}

// ======= REQUIREMENT PREDICATES =======

// R1: Emergency only triggered from Normal mode, by exactly two admins
pred R1 {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Emergency) =>
            (#s.emAdmins = 2 and prevModeIsNormal[s] and all a: s.emAdmins | a in Administrator)
}

// Helper: previous mode is Normal
pred prevModeIsNormal[s: State] {
    some Time/prev[s] and Time/prev[s].mode = Normal
}

// R2: Emergency mode must eventually return to Normal (liveness)
pred R1R2 {
    R1 and
    (all s: State |
        (s.mode = Emergency) =>
            some s2: future[s] | s2.mode = Normal)
}

// R3: Emergency behavior (FIFO bypass, mutual exclusion suspended, em privileges granted)
pred R1R2R3 {
    R1R2 and

    // R3.1: FIFO can be bypassed for high-classification requests
    (all s: State |
        (s.mode = Emergency) => bypassFIFOForHighClass[s])
    and

    // R3.2: Mutual exclusion suspended for all users during Emergency; must be possible for any user to hold any pair of mutually exclusive roles
    (all s: State |
        (s.mode = Emergency) =>
            notMutualExclusionDuringEmergency[s])
    and

    // R3.3: emAdmins have EmergencyPrivilege during Emergency
    (all s: State |
        (s.mode = Emergency) =>
            (all a: s.emAdmins | some ep: s.emPrivs | ep.admin = a and ep.grantedAt = s and no ep.revokedAt))
}

// R3.1 helper: C_High requests may be processed out of order during Emergency
pred bypassFIFOForHighClass[s: State] {
    all r: s.requests |
        (r.classification = C_High) => canBeProcessedOutOfOrder[r, s]
}
pred canBeProcessedOutOfOrder[r: Request, s: State] {
    r in s.requests and s.mode = Emergency and r.classification = C_High
}

// R3.2: No mutual exclusion constraint enforced during Emergency; must be possible for any user to hold any mutually exclusive pair
pred notMutualExclusionDuringEmergency[s: State] {
    // For every user and every pair of mutually exclusive roles, it is permitted to hold both
    all u: User |
        all r1, r2: Role |
            r1 != r2 and r1 in r2.mutuallyExclusiveWith =>
                (r1 = r1)
    // [EVENT]: Fixed Alloy syntax error: replaced (true) with (r1 = r1) to express tautology
}

// Helper: previous mode is Emergency
pred prevModeIsEmergency[s: State] {
    some Time/prev[s] and Time/prev[s].mode = Emergency
}

// R4: Post-Emergency Restoration
pred R1R2R3R4 {
    R1R2R3 and

    // R4.1: emAdmins lose EmergencyPrivilege after Emergency
    (all s: State |
        ((s.mode = Normal and prevModeIsEmergency[s]) =>
            no s.emPrivs))

    and

    // R4.2: Only delegations assigned during Emergency are revoked when Emergency ends
    (all s: State |
        ((s.mode = Normal and prevModeIsEmergency[s]) =>
            all d: Time/prev[s].delegations |
                (d.delegatedAt.mode = Emergency) => (d.expiresAt = s)))

    and

    // R4.2b: Delegations assigned before Emergency are *not* revoked at Emergency end
    (all s: State |
        ((s.mode = Normal and prevModeIsEmergency[s]) =>
            all d: Time/prev[s].delegations |
                (d.delegatedAt.mode = Normal) =>
                    (no d.expiresAt) or (d.expiresAt != s)))

    and

    // R4.3: Only the two emAdmins must update credentials after Emergency
    (all s: State |
        ((s.mode = Normal and prevModeIsEmergency[s]) =>
            (Time/prev[s].emAdmins in s.needsCredentialUpdate and
             all a: s.needsCredentialUpdate | a in Time/prev[s].emAdmins)))
}

// All requirements predicate
pred All_Requirements { R1R2R3R4 }

// ======= ASSERTIONS FOR VERIFICATION =======

// R1: Emergency only by two admins, from Normal mode
assert assertR1 {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Emergency) =>
            (#s.emAdmins = 2 and prevModeIsNormal[s] and all a: s.emAdmins | a in Administrator)
}

// R1b: It is impossible to have Emergency with more/fewer than two admins or not from Normal mode
assert assertR1b_strict {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Emergency) =>
            (#s.emAdmins = 2 and prevModeIsNormal[s])
}

// R2: Emergency mode is always exited (liveness)
assert assertR2 {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Emergency) =>
            some s2: future[s] | s2.mode = Normal
}

// R3: In Emergency, mutual exclusion is suspended for all users (only distinct, mutually exclusive role pairs considered)
assert assertR3 {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Emergency) =>
            all u: User |
                all r1, r2: Role |
                    r1 != r2 and r1 in r2.mutuallyExclusiveWith =>
                        (r1 = r1)
    // [EVENT]: Fixed Alloy syntax error: replaced (true) with (r1 = r1) to express tautology
}

// R3-Strong: It must be possible for at least one user to simultaneously hold two mutually exclusive roles in Emergency
assert assertMutExRolesCanBeHeldEmergency {
    some s: State |
        s.mode = Emergency and
        some u: User, r1, r2: Role |
            r1 != r2 and
            r1 in r2.mutuallyExclusiveWith and
            r1 in rolesHeld[u, s] and r2 in rolesHeld[u, s]
}

// R3-Normal: In Normal mode, no user ever holds two mutually exclusive roles
assert assertNoMutExRolesNormal {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Normal) =>
            all u: User |
                all r1, r2: Role |
                    r1 != r2 and r1 in r2.mutuallyExclusiveWith =>
                        not (r1 in rolesHeld[u, s] and r2 in rolesHeld[u, s])
}

// R4.1: After Emergency, ALL EmergencyPrivileges must be revoked from emAdmins
assert assertR4_1 {
    all s: State |
        ((s.mode = Normal and prevModeIsEmergency[s]) =>
            no s.emPrivs)
}

// R4.2: After Emergency, ONLY Emergency-delegated roles revoked
assert assertR4_2 {
    all s: State |
        ((s.mode = Normal and prevModeIsEmergency[s]) =>
            all d: Time/prev[s].delegations |
                (d.delegatedAt.mode = Emergency) => (d.expiresAt = s))
}

// R4.2b: Delegations assigned before Emergency are NOT revoked at Emergency end
assert assertR4_2b_neg {
    all s: State |
        ((s.mode = Normal and prevModeIsEmergency[s]) =>
            all d: Time/prev[s].delegations |
                (d.delegatedAt.mode = Normal) =>
                    (no d.expiresAt) or (d.expiresAt != s))
}

// R4.3: Only emAdmins must update credentials after Emergency
assert assertR4_3 {
    all s: State |
        ((s.mode = Normal and prevModeIsEmergency[s]) =>
            (Time/prev[s].emAdmins in s.needsCredentialUpdate and
             all a: s.needsCredentialUpdate | a in Time/prev[s].emAdmins))
}

// Strong liveness: Emergency must always eventually return to Normal somewhere in the trace
assert assertEmergencyLiveness {
    all s: State |
        (s.mode = Emergency) =>
            some s2: future[s] | s2.mode = Normal
}

