Thought for 5s
The immediate syntax error is from the standalone and lines after quantified formulas.

In Alloy, this:

all s: State |
  (s.mode = Normal and prevModeIsEmergency[s]) =>
    no s.emPrivs

and
is parsed roughly as if the first all s body keeps going, so Alloy sees something like:

all s: State | condition => no s.emPrivs and and ...
That second and is illegal, which is why the parser points at column 5.

Wrap each quantified clause in parentheses, or use one big block with separate formulas and no explicit top-level ands.

